   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the labor law, in relation to notifying individuals applying\nfor and receiving unemployment benefits of rental assistance and mortgage\nassistance programs",
    "basePrintNo": "S5490",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5490-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §540, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5490\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to notifying individuals\napplying for and receiving unemployment benefits of rental assistance\nand mortgage assistance programs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would require the Department of Labor to notify and provide\ninformation to applicants for unemployment insurance regarding rental\nand mortgage assistance programs available by New York State. The infor-\nmation would also be provided upon every recertification of unemployment\ninsurance and would retroactively include those applying for benefits\nfrom March 1, 2020 and thereafter.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The Commissioner of Labor shall provide a notice to each\nindividual filing a new claim for unemployment benefits and each time an\nindividual recertifies for such benefits informing the individual of\nrental assistance and mortgage assistance programs available through the\ndivision of housing and community renewal and other state agencies. The\nCommissioner shall also provide a link to such programs on the depart-\nment's website. Such link shall be prominently displayed and easily\naccessible by individuals seeking unemployment benefits.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt is imperative that people reaching out for assistance because they\nhave lost their jobs are also provided with other assistance programs\nthat are designed to help keep people in their homes. We also have an\ninterest as a state to be integrated in our approach to connect people\nwith services that will mitigate the situation when people find them-\nselves jobless, especially through no fault of their own as we have seen\nthroughout the COVID-19 pandemic. This legislation will better help\npeople navigate several assistance programs during a challenging time\nfor them and their families.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\nnotice of rental assistance and mortgage assistance programs required\npursuant to section one of this act shall be provided to all individuals\nwho have filed a claim for unemployment benefits on or after March 1,\n2020.\n",
