    "lawCode": "Add §596-a, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5490A\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to notifying individuals\napplying for and receiving unemployment benefits of rental, mortgage,\nfood, and utility assistance programs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would require the Department of Labor to notify and provide\ninformation to applicants for unemployment insurance regarding rental,\nmortgage, food and utility assistance programs available by New York\nState. The information would also be displayed on the Department of\nLabor website upon every certification of unemployment insurance.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: The Commissioner of Labor, in consultation with the Commis-\nsioner of Housing & Community Renewal and the Commissioner of the Office\nof Temporary & Disability Assistance, shall provide a notice to each\nindividual filing a new claim for unemployment benefits informing the\nindividual of rental, mortgage, food and utility assistance programs\navailable through those state agencies.  The Commissioner shall also\nprovide a link to such programs on the department's website and when an\nindividual certifies for unemployment benefits. Such link shall be prom-\ninently displayed and easily accessible by individuals seeking unemploy-\nment benefits.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt is imperative that people reaching out for assistance because they\nhave lost their jobs are also provided with other assistance programs\nthat are designed to help keep people in their homes, combat food inse-\ncurity and keep the lights and heat on in their homes. We also have an\ninterest as a state to be integrated in our approach to connect people\nwith services that will mitigate the situation when people find them-\nselves jobless, especially through no fault of their own as we have seen\nthroughout the COVID-19 pandemic. This legislation will better help\npeople navigate several assistance programs during a challenging time\nfor them and their families.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
