    "lawCode": "Amd §540, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5490B\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to notifying individuals\napplying for and receiving unemployment benefits of rental, mortgage,\nfood, and utility assistance programs\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require the Department of Labor to provide information to unemploy-\nment claimants regarding rental, mortgage, and utility assistance\nprograms available by New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one would require the Commissioner of Labor to provide informa-\ntion on utility assistance and rental and mortgage assistance programs\navailable through the Division of Housing and Community Renewal and the\nOffice of Temporary and Disability Assistance to unemployment insurance\nclaimants. Such information would also be posted on the Department of\nLabor's website.\n\nSection two would establish the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThe amended version moves these provisions into section 540 of the Labor\nLaw.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt is imperative that people reaching out for assistance because they\nhave lost their jobs are also provided with other assistance programs\nthat are designed to help keep people in their homes, combat food inse-\ncurity and keep the lights and heat on in their homes. We also have an\ninterest as a state to be integrated in our approach to connect people\nwith services that will mitigate the situation when people find them-\nselves jobless, especially through no fault of their own as we have seen\nthroughout the COVID-19 pandemic. This legislation will better help\npeople navigate several assistance programs during a challenging time\nfor them and their families.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
